et to finish the level  top tip - if one side of the board seems  locked up use when to move it and create  space win levels are the most unique  feature and farm here is super and they  can be a little bit tough to figure out  since the mechanics are brand new this  tip is reminding us that super saga is  different than any other matching games  we're used to because the pieces on  Winnie levels don't fall toward the  bottom they move in the same direction  of the swipe that we use to make the  match in our clip we can see it is a  link when you level right from the  beginning because the leaves blow across  the screen we're trying to move fij of  the squirrel and the acorn together so  we start making matches in between them  at a point at the point there aren't any  other matches that we can make in  between the two items so we can't get  them closer what are we gonna do we're  gonna have to look outside and make  matches on the outside of that blocked  area create space and change things up  eventually this changes the layout  enough so that we can make a purple  square match which charges fidgets up  and we'll talk about that more in a  later tip and he's able to collect the  acorn  which of which accomplishes our roll  top tip three acorns under the leaves  will always be hidden in the same place  for that level this is pretty  straightforward but it's pretty good to  know at the same time when a level has  leaves on the ground you need to clear  them out to find where the acorns are  that you need to collect sometimes this  can take a few tries to figure out and  so whenever you play this one again  they'll be back in the same place in the  clip we find that there's two acorns at  the bottom of the board we could the  level so we can start from the beginning  again and we find that a chain tube to  pay coins in the exact same position we  could keep playing this level all day  long and that they'll still both be  right there  top tip for matching at the bottom of  the board causes more cascades not to  contradict the game designers here but I  need to mention that this tip applies  specifically to non windy boards this is  a good tip for any match three game with  normal gravity and what's cool is that  if you're playing winning levels you can  actually do this go in any direction  once you get the hang of it so in the  clip you can see that we need to remove  flowers from the top of the board by  making a match at the bottom watch how  the pieces help us out as they fall into  place when the colors filling in the  empty space on the board match up the  flowers get hit and we give that other  matches which help in our collection  top tip 5 try to remove rancid cans as  soon as possible rancid the raccoon is  is up to his old tricks and the beat'em  and super saga we have to make matches  next to his cans which he throws on the  board each time we make a match the can  flips up and hits him and if we do this  enough times he'll get knocked down for  the count in our clip you could see  rancid throws those cans on the board  right away and he'll continue to keep  adding them if you don't start knocking  them back when we hit him with one of  the cans you goes down briefly which  makes it easier for us to focus on  completing our goal top tip 6 in general  removing the static item like flowers or  eyes is the best task to start on first  on different levels you run into oyster  flowers which block the board or cut you  off from being able to collect what you  need so getting them out of it out of  the way will speed things up and it'll  help you get the rest of your collection  so you can beat the level in our clip we  have a ton of flowers and in the way on  this particular board and there's no  real room to make any good match watch  as we clear away the flowers and see how  many different options open up this as  fast as we remove also notice this ties  in with tip 4 as the more space we have  the more you know that has a direct  influence on the number of cascades that  we'll see  top tip seven if you don't beat rancid  he'll come back soon after rancid  doesn't stay on the same levels like he  did in the original farm hero saga  instead he pops up on different parts of  the map and you get one chance to beat  him and collect some coin remember you  have to knock him out and complete the  level to get the corner so our clip  become close to knocking him out and  being the liable but we come up a little  bit short  we were thinking oh well you know that  was close and I really want to earn some  coins but when we look at the map again  the level doesn't have the raccoon on it  anymore don't worry after some time you  will you'll see him hanging out on the  map and he'll be at the bottom left  corner of the screen so you'll know that  he's there and that you can try to beat  him again  top tip 8 in show time you'll get three  moves to collect your super cropsey's so  time is super sagas version of hero mode  if you have three moves left you get  three shots to collect as many  collection points as you can and that  will raise your score if you have a lot  of moves left when you finish the level  you get the extra the extra moves will  like earn you some extra super cropsey's  on the floor and if you have less than  three moves you get to still get to go  you only get like if you have two moves  you'll get to take two extra moves and  you get a chance to clean things up in  our clip you can see that we have a lot  of super cropsey's left and don't want  to have all these points left on the  board sometimes you can't find a match  that will match your supers together  directly so you have to be a little  creative and use matches that will cause  big ones to happen at those extra points  can get you an extra star which  translates into extra growth in the  country show top tip 9 you will always  earn a little bit of growth even if you  don't finish the level growth equals  making coins from the country show and  coins of equal boosters you can use for  tough levels in our clip notice that we  didn't finish the level but even though  we didn't we still earn 5 growth points  for our effort  you  top tip 10 making a super crop see next  to a goat or squirrel will make them  power up as we mentioned earlier super  cropsey's are almost always useful they  can make the squirrel reach further with  his tail when you make make them right  and make the match right next to you the  same goes for the goat except he will  actually jump to a useful spot on the  board so in our clip you'll see that we  have some hay up at the top where we can  we can't you have to collect it but we  can't get to it from the main part of  the board by making a super crop see  right next to the goat it powers them up  and he'll jump to the outside square  where he can collect the hay for us it  should be noted that this is the only  way to get to that square so you don't  want to forget this tip  so those are the top 10 tips from the  farm hero saga team at King Studios in  London I hope this video helped to make  them a little easier to understand  please like the video if you found it  useful and subscribe to my channel to  find all the all the farm heroes super  saga level videos that I put out try to  keep them up to date and if you need  help you can always find it there I want  to thank the King team for putting these  tips together and I'll be posting more  helpful videos based on their content in  the near future thanks for watching talk  to you soon
 

